Bitcoin Market Sentiment & Trader Performance Analysis
A quantitative research project analyzing how Bitcoin market sentiment influences trader behavior and profitability using historical trading data and the Crypto Fear & Greed Index.

Highlights
Performed advanced EDA and sentiment-based trader analysis
Engineered trader-level risk and profitability features
Built KMeans clustering models to identify trader archetypes
Applied Machine Learning models for profitable trade prediction
Created interactive and professional visualizations using Plotly

Tech Stack
Python
Pandas & NumPy
Matplotlib & Seaborn
Plotly
Scikit-learn
XGBoost
SHAP

Key Insights
Trader profitability changes significantly across Fear vs Greed market phases
High leverage usage increases during Extreme Greed periods

Certain trader clusters consistently outperform others on a risk-adjusted basis
